# THE FUSIONS OF ONE PART THAT ELIMINATE NOTHING, BESIDE THE PART THEY CARRY. One row per such
# fusion per quantity, with the part's figure and the composed figure side by side.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ IDENTITY IS THE ONE CASE WHERE COMPOSITION NEEDS NO ARITHMETIC AT ALL, which is what
#    makes it the sharpest test in the file. A fusion of one part that eliminates nothing must
#    reproduce that part: there is nothing to sum, nothing to subtract, and no judgement to
#    make. So any difference is a defect with no defence, and it can be asked of EVERY quantity
#    rather than only the one the sum rule composes.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND THAT IS FIVE QUANTITIES AGAINST THE SUM RULE'S ONE. `checks/fusion_sum_disagrees`
#    reads `composition/fused.sqlc`, which answers `'demand' AS quantity` as a literal;
#    `checks/window_lost_or_summed` covers the calendar. Nothing composes a nameplate or any of
#    the three buffer slacks, and the corpus files SIX SIZED `nameplate` eliminations and TWO
#    `draw` ones that no relation reads. A composer did the work and nothing consumed it.
#
# ⚠️ A ONE-PART FUSION IS NOT DEGENERATE, and `every-local-part` says so in its own words:
#    "A one-part fusion is not degenerate: it says this reviewer read that layer and carried
#    it." Carrying is an assertion, so it is a thing that can be got wrong.
#
# ⭐ THE FACTOR STILL APPLIES. A single part may be converted into the composed layer's unit,
#   so identity is "the part, converted" rather than "the part, copied".
#
# ⛔⛔ AND A FACTOR FILED AS ABSENT IS EXCLUDED RATHER THAN READ AS ONE. `coalesce(factor, 1)`
#    is the fill this directory warns about wherever it appears: 1 is the multiplicative
#    identity, and filling an absence with an identity element is only sound where the absence
#    means MEASURED AND EMPTY. `asrt:factor` is a `pm:StatedClaim`, so its absent arm carries a
#    typed reason, and `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files `unmeasured` on one of
#    its parts -- a composer saying nobody measured the conversion. Read as 1 that becomes "the
#    units are the same", which is a claim they declined to make. Identity cannot be asserted
#    across a conversion nobody sized, so those parts leave this relation.
#
# ⚠️ THE OMITTED ELEMENT IS A DIFFERENT STATE AND IT STAYS. `minOccurs="0"` and no factor means
#    no conversion is needed, which is the sender asserting the units already agree. That is a
#    filing; `unmeasured` is a gap.
-- asrt:Fusion with one asrt:Part and no asrt:elimination, against layers/quantities.sqlc.
SELECT p.composition AS filing, p.composed_layer AS layer, part.quantity,
       part.low  * coalesce(p.factor_low,  1) AS part_low,
       part.mode * coalesce(p.factor_mode, 1) AS part_mode,
       part.high * coalesce(p.factor_high, 1) AS part_high,
       part.unit AS part_unit,
       filed.low AS filed_low, filed.mode AS filed_mode, filed.high AS filed_high,
       filed.unit AS filed_unit
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
) p
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/quantities.sqlc)
) part ON part.filing = p.part_filing AND part.layer = p.part_layer
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/quantities.sqlc)
) filed ON filed.filing = p.composition AND filed.layer = p.composed_layer
       AND filed.quantity = part.quantity
WHERE p.factor_absent IS NULL
  AND (p.composition, p.composed_layer) IN (
        SELECT composition, composed_layer
        FROM ( :compose(composition/parts.sqlc) ) one
        GROUP BY composition, composed_layer
        HAVING count(*) = 1)
  AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM ( :compose(eliminations/filed.sqlc) ) e
        WHERE e.composition = p.composition AND e.composed_layer = p.composed_layer)
  AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM ( :compose(composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc) ) s
        WHERE s.composition = p.composition AND s.composed_layer = p.composed_layer)
